          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life</strong><br>\nNeil Armstrong was born on August 5, 1930, in Wapakoneta, Ohio. As a child, he developed a passion for aviation and earned his pilot's license before his driver's license.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Navy Service</strong><br>\nArmstrong studied aeronautical engineering at Purdue University on a U.S. Navy scholarship and served as a naval aviator from 1949 to 1952.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Test Pilot Career</strong><br>\nAfter completing his service, Armstrong joined the National Advisory Committee for Aeronautics (NACA), which later became NASA. He tested many high-speed aircraft, including the X-15, which could reach the edge of space.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Joining the Astronaut Corps</strong><br>\nArmstrong was selected as an astronaut by NASA in 1962 and first flew on Gemini 8, achieving the first successful docking of two spacecraft in orbit.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Apollo 11 Mission</strong><br>\nOn July 16, 1969, Armstrong commanded the Apollo 11 mission and on July 20, he became the first person to walk on the moon, with the famous words, \"That's one small step for [a] man, one giant leap for mankind.\"</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Life and Legacy</strong><br>\nAfter retiring from NASA in 1971, Armstrong taught at the University of Cincinnati and served on the boards of several companies.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
